TITLE: YGGDRASIL — DEVELOPMENTAL SUBSTRATE V0
DATE: 2026-09-22
STATUS: FROZEN HAND-DESIGNED SUBSTRATE FOR FIRST TASK-BEARING EXPERIMENT
TRACK: DG-1 / APPLICATION-A TRANSITION

PURPOSE

Freeze the hand-designed cellular substrate
at the end of the abstract periodic-stability program
so Task 1 measures functional behavior
without continuing to tune the pulse benchmark.

This record is a substrate boundary.
It is not a learned NCA updater,
not a new periodic-stability experiment,
and not authorization for A54-style tuning.

CLOSURE BASIS

A45 established the inherited ECHO_PHASE substrate
and showed that a one-epoch cooperative support echo
is mechanically active, strongly improves local core survival,
and remains reversible,
even though it does not by itself solve the 5:3 macro oscillator.

A48 established G5_FULL as a reproducible MODERATE
recovery aid across five fresh manifests.
It is retained as an optional validated recovery mechanism,
not a universal default.

A49 established that challenge-phase periphery push/pull
is mechanically active but does not produce sufficient macro information gain.
It is not part of the V0 default substrate.

A51 challenge-field TTL memory is not retained in V0.

A52 established response phase as a real causal axis,
but fixed TAU3 delay trades transient persistence
against genuine-reversal responsiveness.
Fixed phase memory is not retained in V0.

A53 established that current-evidence veto
restores reversal safety but destroys the useful TAU3 transient-challenge benefit.
TAU3_VETO is not retained in V0.

