V0 CORE CELL-STATE CONTRACT

The V0 hand-designed cell lineage retains the existing bounded state family:

C:
committed C side.

S:
committed S side.

U:
uncommitted / recruitable.

H:
hedged / uncertainty state.

FC / FS:
side-specific refractory states.

The substrate retains:

signed local evidence state B;

commitment age / refractory timing;

local neighborhood evidence;

local cooperative support state needed by A45 ECHO_PHASE;

one-epoch side-specific Q trace;

bounded local recruitment / defection semantics;

explicit state-transition telemetry.

No global majority label,
context/family identifier,
future environment,
or centralized confidence scalar
enters the cell update rule.

FROZEN LOCAL EVIDENCE / UPDATE SEMANTICS

Preserve the inherited A45 ECHO_PHASE contract:

rho = 3/4 for signed evidence accumulation;

local evidence radius = 12;

Hill n = 3;

Hill K = 1/2;

cooperative / recruitment radius = 3;

A44 support recruitment ETA = 1/2;

D2 and D3 refractory families remain
separate frozen substrate variants.

Task 1 must select its D family
before primary execution.
It may not choose D2 versus D3
post-result.

ONE-EPOCH COOPERATIVE SUPPORT ECHO

Preserve exact A45 behavior:

Q_eff = max(Q_raw, Q_echo).

The trace stores current Q_raw only.

It never stores Q_eff.

It is one epoch only.

It is side-specific.

It resets when commitment is lost.

It cannot cross commitment side.

New commitments begin echo-free.

There is:

no trace gain;

no trace decay coefficient;

no recursive memory-of-memory;

no global phase input;

no future read.

This mechanism is retained because
it is a demonstrated local causal mechanism
that approximately doubled third-hit core persistence
without creating reversal lock-in.

TOPOLOGY CONTRACT

V0 uses a fixed bounded local topology.

No open-ended growth.

No dynamic edge creation.

No global dense attention.

No centralized planner.

Any Task 1 topology change
must be preregistered as a separate factor
and may not be mixed with substrate tuning.

OPTIONAL VALIDATED RECOVERY LAYER

G5_FULL status:
VALIDATED OPTIONAL / MODERATE.

A48 result:
robust across five fresh manifests;
strong threshold not met.

D3 pooled unresolved-duration reduction:
approximately 19.08%.

D3 pooled favored-majority recovery-latency improvement:
approximately 0.910 epoch.

D2 pooled unresolved-duration reduction:
approximately 9.28%.

D2 pooled recovery-latency improvement:
approximately 0.388 epoch.

G5_FULL may be included in Task 1 only if:

its inclusion is preregistered before execution;

its frozen implementation is used unchanged;

no recovery threshold, dose, timer, probability, or gate is retuned.

DEFAULT V0:
G5_FULL OFF unless the Task 1 preregistration explicitly enables it.

EXCLUDED / UNVALIDATED OPTIONAL MECHANISMS

The following are NOT part of the Task 1 default substrate:

A49 challenge push-pull;

A51 challenge-field TTL memory;

A52 fixed response delay / TAU3 phase memory;

A53 current-evidence-vetoed phase memory.

They remain research evidence,
not default developmental primitives.

Phase sensitivity itself remains
an established empirical property,
but no tested phase-memory controller
is validated for V0.

TASK 1 INTERFACE BOUNDARY

Task 1 may add only the minimum task interface required to measure useful function:

immutable/local task input channels;

a preregistered output/readout contract;

task-specific external scoring;

additional telemetry that does not alter dynamics.

Task 1 may not silently change:

cell-state meanings;

B update semantics;

ECHO_PHASE semantics;

refractory semantics;

local radii;

Hill law;

recruitment law;

randomness namespaces;

topology;

or optional-mechanism status.

If a task requires one of those changes,
that change must be isolated in a later preregistered experiment.

ANTI-ORACLE / DECENTRALIZATION CONTRACT

No task solution may depend on:

a hidden full-world controller;

global majority injected into local state;

future task labels;

context or family IDs used as shortcuts;

restoring a saved full phenotype after damage;

or a sequential RNG cursor that makes treatment identity change inherited randomness.

Task scoring may be global externally.
Cell decisions remain local under the declared contract.

REPRODUCIBILITY CONTRACT

Every Task 1 scientific run must bind before execution:

exact source identity;

exact task manifest;

world / sample count;

seed(s);

D-family selection;

G5_FULL ON/OFF;

readout definition;

success / failure thresholds;

integrity probes.

Primary execution must be duplicated byte-identically
before scientific interpretation where deterministic execution is expected.

DEFERRED MECHANISMS

V0 does not require:

a learned NCA updater;

richer communication protocol;

dynamic topology;

long-term role DNA;

Byzantine-cell machinery;

resource economy;

open-ended replication;

neural-module payloads;

LoRA / micro-expert cells.

Those remain deferred until task evidence requires them.

