NEXT STEP

Resolve and preregister the first task-bearing environment.

Use V0 unchanged for the first task run.

Do not reopen pulse-world tuning
merely because Task 1 exposes a new failure.
A task-specific failure should first be diagnosed
as task interface, readout, learning, communication,
or substrate limitation before changing V0.

PLAIN-SPEAK SUMMARY

We are done teaching the organism
how to survive one artificial pulse pattern.

We now have a frozen local organism
with a real one-step cooperative memory,
reasonable reversal behavior,
and an optional recovery aid
whose benefit reproduced across fresh worlds.

The later tricks we tested
changed behavior,
but none earned a place
in the default organism.

So Task 1 starts from the organism we actually proved,
not from another round of pulse-specific knobs.

The next question is no longer:

"can we make the pulse chart look better?"

It is:

"can this frozen local organism do useful work?"

